  "question": {
    "text": "A hydrocarbon &#39;X&#39; with formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;uses two moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;on catalystic hydrogenation of its one mole. On ozonolysis, &#39;X&#39; yields two moles of methane dicarbaldehyde. The hydrocarbon &#39;X&#39; is :"
  },
